% added on 2026-09-16 and checked the same day against the publisher's own record, the
% metadata each publisher deposits with Crossref when it registers the DOI: MolVisGNN (Wiley),
% AMCT (ACM), SCAGE (Springer Nature), Bemis-Murcko (ACS), BRICS (Wiley), Platt (MIT Press)
% and Optuna (ACM). That check corrected one entry, Platt, whose title and year as commonly
% cited do not match the published chapter; see the note beside it. Nothing is guessed. The
% same list appears in human-readable form at the end of paper/draft.md; if you edit one,
% edit both.
%
% main.tex cites these with \cite{...} and typesets them with \bibliographystyle{unsrt}, so
% entries are numbered by order of first citation. scripts/make_latex.py refuses to build if
% the draft's own numbering disagrees with that order.
%
% Keep `note` fields bibliographic. BibTeX prints them in the reference list, so a reminder
% left in one ("cite the corrected version") appears in the published paper. Reminders about
% an entry belong in a % comment beside it.

